Looks like in rpubs.R, there's a call to deploymentRecord that's missing some arguments.

@adamconroy ?

This is needed in order to solve https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/141.

Last week, I talked to Joe about that bug and he thought that we'd already supplied this information, because the header `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` should be included in `session$request` (see test app at the bottom). However, when we actually tried it, that's not happening (this a problem across the board: it's not in SSOS, SSP, shinyapps.io or Connect...)

I've filed a similar issue for shiny-server (https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-server/issues/324) that includes a potential solution, but that probably won't apply here since I'm guessing that the internals of these two repos are totally different.

Another detail: it's important to make sure that `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` is present in the server (i.e. inside `session$request`) and not only in the ui (i.e. inside the `req` arg which is present if the UI is a function with that argument). 

Here's the test app: https://beta.rstudioconnect.com/content/3126/. It prints out both the ui's `req` elements and the server's `session$request` elements. (Finally, it also checks if `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` is present in the server and prints it out, otherwise defaulting to `REMOTE_ADDR` -- this last bit is basically what we should suggest for  https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/141 once this is fixed.)

<details>
  <summary>app.R (source code)</font></summary>

```r
library(shiny)

ui_xfwd <- NULL

ui <- function(req) {
  if ("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR" %in% ls(req)) ui_xfwd <<- req[["HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR"]]
  fluidPage(
    h3("UI req"),
    paste(ls(req), collapse = " "),
    h3("server session$request"),
    textOutput("request"),
    h3("result"),
    uiOutput("result")
  )
}

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  output$request <- renderText({
    paste(ls(session$request), collapse = " ")
  })
  
  output$result <- renderUI({
    if ("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR" %in% ls(session$request)) {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header present in server:"),
        p(session$request[["HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR"]])
      )
    } else if (!is.null(ui_xfwd)) {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header present in UI:"),
        p(ui_xfwd)
      )
    } else {
      div(
        p("HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR header not present in UI or server; here's the REMOTE_ADDR:"),
        p(session$request[["REMOTE_ADDR"]])
      )
    }
  })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

</details>
<br/>

_Edit_: change `HTTP_X_FORWARDED` to `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR` and updated app
